        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0415" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1474.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-12T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1915—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After conference with the Dominican Minister here we ask you to make the
                    following suggestion to President Jiménes: Internal revenue stamps given away or
                    sold at a big discount will, if used, very much reduce the revenue from internal
                    revenue sources. We advise, therefore, that the President issue a proclamation
                    declaring the old stamps invalid and non-receivable, at the same time offering
                    to redeem outstanding stamps at the price paid for them plus legal rate of
                    interest from date of purchase. This will give internal revenue at once and from
                    the money thus received the old stamps can be redeemed, the burden of proof
                    being upon those presenting stamps for redemption to show the amount actually
                    paid for them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
